### VULN-029 — Seat/plan-cap over-provision race (TOCTOU)
### Setup: a BASIC (cap 20) org filled to 19 active students (1 seat left).
### Fire K concurrent accepts on DISTINCT invite links (so they don't serialize on the
### invite-row lock), racing the org-row capacity check that is NOT held across the insert:
POST http://localhost:21527/invite/r/<distinct-token-1>/accept   # joiner 1  ┐
POST http://localhost:21527/invite/r/<distinct-token-2>/accept   # joiner 2  │ fired
...                                                              #           │ simultaneously
POST http://localhost:21527/invite/r/<distinct-token-K>/accept   # joiner K  ┘
Origin: http://localhost:21526
Cookie: classroomio.session_token=<each joiner's session>
### Vulnerable: assertStudentCapacityOrThrow() runs on autocommit `db` (student-limit.ts:86),
### invoked WITHOUT the accept `tx` (invite-link.ts:242) → lock released before member insert.
### On this fast local Postgres the check→commit window did not open (1 succeeded); see notes.md.
